00:07:26.870 --> 00:07:29.150
Where is conversational
commerce going?

00:07:29.150 --> 00:07:31.910
You hear a lot of people say,
well, I've got my Google Home,

00:07:31.910 --> 00:07:34.850
and it does my kid's
homework, or it tells me

00:07:34.850 --> 00:07:35.930
the news in the morning.

00:07:35.930 --> 00:07:38.810
It plays music, but
really, it's not

00:07:38.810 --> 00:07:40.770
going to do anything
more for me.

00:07:40.770 --> 00:07:43.520
However, if we think
about the way trends have

00:07:43.520 --> 00:07:48.830
gone in the past, just by a
quick scan of our group here

00:07:48.830 --> 00:07:50.660
today, most of you
probably have never

00:07:50.660 --> 00:07:54.410
had a television in your home
without a remote control.

00:07:54.410 --> 00:07:57.200
You couldn't really think
about getting up off the couch

00:07:57.200 --> 00:07:59.330
right now and
changing that channel.

00:07:59.330 --> 00:08:02.210
And that's exactly what people
said when remote controls first

00:08:02.210 --> 00:08:02.953
came out.

00:08:02.953 --> 00:08:05.120
Why would I have to have
this thing, when I can just

00:08:05.120 --> 00:08:06.830
get up and change a knob?

00:08:06.830 --> 00:08:08.510
Well, most of us
would never even

00:08:08.510 --> 00:08:11.010
think about turning
a knob anymore.

00:08:11.010 --> 00:08:12.830
In fact, most of
us, or a lot of us,

00:08:12.830 --> 00:08:16.460
now use the little microphone
on our remote control.

00:08:16.460 --> 00:08:18.560
So you can see how
things suddenly become

00:08:18.560 --> 00:08:21.260
adapted and part of our life.

00:08:21.260 --> 00:08:22.532
Same thing with cell phones.

00:08:22.532 --> 00:08:23.990
When cell phones
first came out, we

00:08:23.990 --> 00:08:26.840
had a PDF Palm
Pilot, which kept all

00:08:26.840 --> 00:08:29.960
of our contacts
and our pictures.

00:08:29.960 --> 00:08:32.240
And people said,
you know, I can't

00:08:32.240 --> 00:08:35.020
imagine having a
phone and my contacts

00:08:35.020 --> 00:08:36.933
and calendar device
in one thing.

00:08:36.933 --> 00:08:38.600
And I have to talk,
then I have to look.

00:08:38.600 --> 00:08:39.392
And I have to talk.

00:08:39.392 --> 00:08:41.210
It seems ridiculous.

00:08:41.210 --> 00:08:42.740
Well now, I don't
think any of us

00:08:42.740 --> 00:08:45.590
would really consider having two
separate devices for something

00:08:45.590 --> 00:08:46.640
like that.

00:08:46.640 --> 00:08:49.070
Same holds true for
conversational commerce

00:08:49.070 --> 00:08:50.840
in people's homes.

00:08:50.840 --> 00:08:54.500
You're seeing more and more
people take their Google Home

00:08:54.500 --> 00:08:58.670
device or other device and
connect it to their lights,

00:08:58.670 --> 00:09:02.030
to their furnace systems,
their AC systems, their garage

00:09:02.030 --> 00:09:03.510
doors, what have you.

00:09:03.510 --> 00:09:06.260
So it's starting to
move forward that way.

00:09:06.260 --> 00:09:09.020
As a result, what we're
seeing is our clients

00:09:09.020 --> 00:09:11.810
are really trying to
capture that and work

00:09:11.810 --> 00:09:14.240
with their clients so
that they can get to know

00:09:14.240 --> 00:09:16.220
who their end clients are.

00:09:16.220 --> 00:09:19.650
This is important
because, as you can see,

00:09:19.650 --> 00:09:23.023
people are starting to order
things from their devices.

00:09:23.023 --> 00:09:24.440
The other thing
that's interesting

00:09:24.440 --> 00:09:27.980
is that devices that
have been developed

00:09:27.980 --> 00:09:31.110
have sort of a
personality, if you will,

00:09:31.110 --> 00:09:34.190
based on how they were
developed to begin with.

00:09:34.190 --> 00:09:35.400
The Google Home device--

00:09:35.400 --> 00:09:40.370
you know, Google itself was
developed on a platform that

00:09:40.370 --> 00:09:42.830
was a search engine.

00:09:42.830 --> 00:09:45.680
So what you see is
that there is a lot

00:09:45.680 --> 00:09:49.040
that you can leverage when
you're developing on a Google

00:09:49.040 --> 00:09:50.210
Home platform.

00:09:50.210 --> 00:09:52.160
There is a wealth
of data out there,

00:09:52.160 --> 00:09:54.950
location services, et
cetera, as well as the APIs

00:09:54.950 --> 00:09:56.790
that you can
leverage from Google,

00:09:56.790 --> 00:10:01.790
which make it very easy to then
bring this into people's homes.

00:10:01.790 --> 00:10:04.370
What we're seeing
in terms of trends

00:10:04.370 --> 00:10:08.240
is that not only are people
starting to develop and adapt

00:10:08.240 --> 00:10:13.670
to digital and conversational
commerce, but what we're seeing

00:10:13.670 --> 00:10:17.660
is that eventually we'll have
what we call a digital twin.

00:10:17.660 --> 00:10:20.330
That digital device
will know you so well,

00:10:20.330 --> 00:10:24.320
it will know your
moods, your birthdays,

00:10:24.320 --> 00:10:26.060
your kids' birthdays.

00:10:26.060 --> 00:10:29.660
And it will soon replace what
used to be the shopkeeper down

00:10:29.660 --> 00:10:30.690
the street.

00:10:30.690 --> 00:10:34.580
Long ago, a shopkeeper down
the street knew you by name.

00:10:34.580 --> 00:10:37.820
They knew when
you came in to buy

00:10:37.820 --> 00:10:41.630
your bread, your wine, whatever
it was, if you had a bad day.

00:10:41.630 --> 00:10:45.200
They knew if you celebrated
Hanukkah, Diwali, or Christmas,

00:10:45.200 --> 00:10:47.720
or whatever it was
that you celebrated,

00:10:47.720 --> 00:10:50.930
so that then they would prepare
their products accordingly.

00:10:50.930 --> 00:10:53.840
Same holds true with
conversational commerce.

00:10:53.840 --> 00:10:55.760
What we're seeing is
that it's becoming

00:10:55.760 --> 00:10:59.420
a part of people's lives so
much that it will eventually

00:10:59.420 --> 00:11:03.920
develop a digital twin for you,
so that it will automatically

00:11:03.920 --> 00:11:08.660
take care of things for you that
you may not have expected it to

00:11:08.660 --> 00:11:09.930
in the past.

00:11:09.930 --> 00:11:13.130
So that's what we're seeing
from a personal perspective.

00:11:13.130 --> 00:11:16.070
What we're seeing from
an industry perspective

00:11:16.070 --> 00:11:20.360
is that companies are going
to start shifting not just

00:11:20.360 --> 00:11:24.680
to providing services and
information to their consumer

00:11:24.680 --> 00:11:28.070
on the front end, but leveraging
conversational commerce

00:11:28.070 --> 00:11:31.790
on the back end so that they
can reduce costs in supply

00:11:31.790 --> 00:11:36.740
chain, manufacturing,
training, and things like that,

00:11:36.740 --> 00:11:39.230
in conjunction
with the AI and IoT

00:11:39.230 --> 00:11:41.640
that they can couple with that.

00:11:41.640 --> 00:11:44.150
So these are some of the
trends that we're seeing,

00:11:44.150 --> 00:11:46.190
going forward.

00:11:46.190 --> 00:11:49.340
As I mentioned, and what John
will show you in just a moment,

00:11:49.340 --> 00:11:51.350
is that we partner
with our clients

00:11:51.350 --> 00:11:55.070
to solve for various solutions
